tive to '2's. It seems the relationship (col - row - c) % 4 == 0 holds true. I have confirmed that for r <= c, the 1's are *strictly* between the 2's, which I can now formalize. And I'm now certain about the condition that r must be at least 3 for a 1 to appear. I am now exploring if a simplified expression will capture this.\n\n\n**Formalizing the Rule**\n\nI've been working to formalize the rule about where '1's appear relative to '2's. I can confirm the `(col - row - c) % 4 == 0` expression holds true. Specifically, no '1' appears between the two '2's for rows r <= c. I'm now certain, that r must be at least 3 for a 1 to appear. The rule works across all cases, and I am quite certain it is now correct. I have decided to cease further refinement to move on.\n\n\n",
